Stop also assembling the snapshot blob when clang-cl takes the C++ route

mksnapshot writes the snapshot blob as a pair of files: snapshot.cc and embedded.S,
and the v8_snapshot target marks both as sources, so both are compiled. For Windows
with clang-cl, V8 additionally defines an asm_to_inline_asm action that converts
embedded.S into embedded.cc, and that C++ file is the one meant to be compiled -
embedded.S is written in the assembler syntax gcc and clang use, which MASM's ml64
cannot read. Under ninja on Windows both routes are built, and the build stops at the
assembler:

    ASM obj\tools\v8_gypfiles\v8_snapshot.gen\v8_snapshot.embedded_asm.obj
    embedded.S(1) : error A2008:syntax error : /
    embedded.S(10) : error A2034:must be in segment block

Even if ml64 could read it, the blob symbols would then be defined twice - once in
embedded.obj, once in embedded_asm.obj - and both objects are listed in v8_snapshot.lib.

So in that configuration the mksnapshot action stops contributing its outputs as
sources, and snapshot.cc is listed on the target instead. embedded.cc keeps arriving
through the asm_to_inline_asm action, which still marks its own output as a source.

Nothing changes for gcc/clang on Linux and macOS, where embedded.S really is assembled,
and nothing changes for cl.exe without clang-cl, where no .cc replacement is generated.

--- a/tools/v8_gypfiles/v8.gyp
+++ b/tools/v8_gypfiles/v8.gyp
@@ -438,6 +438,14 @@
           ],
           'process_outputs_as_sources': 1,
           'conditions': [
+            # With clang-cl the blob goes to the C++ compiler instead: the
+            # asm_to_inline_asm action on this target turns embedded.S into a .cc.
+            # Assembling the .S as well would define the same symbols twice, and
+            # ml64 cannot read the file's syntax anyway. The C++ output of this
+            # action is listed on the target instead.
+            ['OS=="win" and clang==1', {
+              'process_outputs_as_sources': 0,
+            }],
             ['v8_random_seed', {
               'variables': {
                 'mksnapshot_flags': ['--random-seed', '<(v8_random_seed)'],
@@ -532,6 +540,9 @@
